The mapping example for `sys_comment` → `FeedItem[]` doesn’t match the Console implementation: the record uses `id` (not `_id`), comment text is stored under `content` (not `body`), `author` is an object (so `actor` should be derived from `author.name`), and reactions are persisted as an emoji->userIds map that must be converted to `Reaction[]` (count + reacted) for the UI. Please adjust the example to reflect these field names and the reaction conversion logic.
```suggestion
// Current viewer's user id (from your auth/session layer)
const currentUserId = /* get current user id */ '';

// Helper: convert emoji -> userIds map into Reaction[]
const toReactions = (
  reactionMap: Record<string, string[]> | undefined,
  userId: string,
): Reaction[] => {
  if (!reactionMap) return [];

  return Object.entries(reactionMap).map(([emoji, userIds]) => ({
    emoji,
    count: userIds.length,
    reacted: !!userId && userIds.includes(userId),
  }));
};

// Map to FeedItem[]
const feedItems: FeedItem[] = comments.map(c => ({
  id: c.id,
  type: 'comment',
  actor: c.author?.name,
  body: c.content,
  createdAt: c.createdAt,
  reactions: toReactions(c.reactions, currentUserId),
```
